# Routes and layout

Define routes in `src/routes/index.tsx`. Keep path strings in `src/routes/paths.ts`.

- `/` redirects to `/dashboard`
- `/login` renders `LoginPage` with no dashboard shell
- `/dashboard` renders inside `DashboardLayout`

```tsx
<Route element={<DashboardLayout />}>
  <Route path={paths.dashboard} element={<DashboardPage />} />
</Route>
```

Split the dashboard shell into small components under `src/layout/`. Do not merge them back into one file.

- `DashboardLayout` — sidebar beside a column of header and main
- `Sidebar` — `Logo` and `NavLinks`
- `NavLinks` — `NavLink` items from `paths`
- `Header` — top bar
- `MainContent` — `<Outlet />` for the matched page
- `Loader` — Suspense fallback and `hydrateFallbackElement`
- `ErrorBoundary` — wraps the router; `RouteErrorBoundary` is the route `errorElement`
